icantly by 112.94 U.S. Do\nollar per Ounce 24K).\nThe gold gram recorded 145.96 \nice Today in U.S. Dollar (USD)\nGold Unit Current Pri","content":"Gold Price in U.S. Dollar Sunday, 17 May 2026\nLast update: Sunday, 17 May 2026, 12:10 AM, GMT time. Physical gold sales\nGold price today, Sunday, 17 May 2026 has decreased significantly by 112.94 U.S. Dollar per Ounce 24K to reach 4,539.37 U.S. Dollar per Ounce 24K (change percent of -2.43% compared to yesterday rate of 4,652.31 U.S. Dollar per Ounce 24K).\nThe gold gram recorded 145.96 U.S. Dollar for karat 24, 133.80 U.S. Dollar for karat 22, 127.72 U.S. Dollar for karat 21, and 109.47 U.S. Dollar for karat 18.\nGold Price Today in U.S. Dollar (USD)\nGold Unit Current Price Previous Price Change Percent\nGold Ounce 4,539.37 4,652.31  -2.43%\nGold Gram 24K 145.96 149.59\nGold Gram 23K 140.85 144.36\nGold Gram 22K 133.70 137.03\nGold Gram 21K 127.72 130.89\nGold Gram 18K 109.47 112.19\nGold Gram 14K 85.39 87.51\nGold Gram 12K 72.98 74.80\nGold Gram 10K 60.87 62.38\nGold Gram 9K 54.74 56.10\nGold Gram 8K 48.60 49.81\nGold Price Chart in U.S. Dollar\nGold Price in U.S. Dollar in the last month\nDate Gold Ounce Gold Gram 24K Gold Gram 22K Gold Gram 21K Gold Gram 18K\n16 May 2026 4,539.37 145.96 133.70 127.72 109.47\n15 May 2026 4,566.21 146.82 134.49 128.47 110.12\n14 May 2026 4,672.90 150.25 137.63 131.47 112.69\n13 May 2026 4,694.84 150.96 138.28 132.09 113.22\n12 May 2026 4,672.90 150.25 137.63 131.47 112.69\n11 May 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n10 May 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n9 May 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n8 May 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n7 May 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n6 May 2026 4,694.84 150.96 138.28 132.09 113.22\n5 May 2026 4,566.21 146.82 134.49 128.47 110.12\n4 May 2026 4,524.89 145.49 133.27 127.31 109.12\n3 May 2026 4,608.29 148.18 135.73 129.65 111.13\n2 May 2026 4,608.29 148.18 135.73 129.65 111.13\n1 May 2026 4,629.63 148.86 136.36 130.25 111.65\n30 Apr 2026 4,608.29 148.18 135.73 129.65 111.13\n29 Apr 2026 4,545.45 146.16 133.88 127.89 109.62\n28 Apr 2026 4,587.16 147.50 135.11 129.06 110.62\n27 Apr 2026 4,672.90 150.25 137.63 131.47 112.69\n26 Apr 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n25 Apr 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n24 Apr 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n23 Apr 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n22 Apr 2026 4,739.34 152.39 139.59 133.34 114.29\n21 Apr 2026 4,716.98 151.67 138.93 132.71 113.75\n20 Apr 2026 4,807.69 154.59 141.60 135.26 115.94\n19 Apr 2026 4,830.92 155.33 142.29 135.92 116.50\n18 Apr 2026 4,830.92 155.33 142.29 135.92 116.50\n17 Apr 2026 4,854.37 156.09 142.98 136.58 117.07\n16 Apr 2026 4,784.69 153.85 140.93 134.62 115.39\nFrequently Asked Questions\nWhat is the gold rate today Sunday, 17 May 2026?\nAs of Sunday, 17 May 2026, the gold price today is 4,539.37 U.S. Dollar per ounce. The 24K gold rate is 145.96 U.S. Dollar per gram, while 22K and 21K are priced at 133.80 and 127.72 respectively. Dollar currency forecast\nWhat is the current gold price per ounce in USD Sunday, 17 May 2026?\nThe current gold price per ounce in USD as of Sunday, 17 May 2026 is 4,539.37 USD. This reflects the live spot price, which can fluctuate throughout the day based on market conditions.\nWhat is the current gold price per gram in USD Sunday, 17 May 2026?\nThe current gold price per ounce in USD as of Sunday, 17 May 2026 is 145.96 USD. This is the price for 24K gold per gram, which is the purest form of gold. The prices for 22K and 21K gold per gram are 133.80 USD and 127.72 USD respectively.\nWhat is the difference between the 'Bid' and 'Ask' price?\nThe 'Bid' is the highest price a buyer (like a dealer) is willing to pay for your gold. The 'Ask' is the lowest price a seller is willing to accept. When you buy gold, you pay the Ask price plus a premium; when you sell, you typically receive the Bid price. The difference between the two is known as the 'spread'.\nWhy has gold reached record highs in 2026?\nGold's surge toward the $5,000-$5,400 range in 2026 is driven by several structural factors: record-level buying by central banks, persistent global inflation, and the 'scarcity loop' as mine production remains flat at 1-2% growth. Additionally, new tariffs on gold imports in certain regions have added upward pressure on local retail prices.\nWhat is a 'Troy Ounce' and how does it differ from a standard ounce?\nGold is measured in 'Troy Ounces,' which are heavier than standard (avoirdupois) ounces used for groceries. One troy ounce equals exactly 31.103 grams, whereas a standard ounce is approximately 28.35 grams. Always ensure you are using the troy measurement when calculating investment value. Gram silver prices\nShould I buy physical gold or Gold ETFs?\nPhysical gold (bars and coins) offers direct ownership with no counterparty risk, making it a favorite for 'crisis hedging.' Gold ETFs (Exchange-Traded Funds) track the price of gold without requiring physical storage, offering higher liquidity and ease of trading for those focused on price speculation rather than long-term possession.\nDoes the gold price include 'Premiums'?\nNo, the live spot price you see on charts represents the raw value of the metal. When purchasing retail products like 'Gold Eagles' or 'PAMP Bars,' dealers add a 'premium' to cover manufacturing, insurance, and their profit margin. In 2026, premiums have stayed elevated due to high physical demand and supply chain constraints.\nGold Performance USD/Ounce 24K Silver ounce tracker\nPeriod Change Change %\n1 Day -112.94 -2.43%\n1 Week -177.61 -3.77%\n30 Days -245.32 -5.13%\n6 Months +457.74 +11.21%\n1 Year +1,354.66 +42.54%\n5 Years +2,690.94 +145.58%\n10 Years +3,260.60 +254.98%\nGold Calculator\nMetal\nKarat\n24K (.999)\nWeight\n1\nUnit\nOunce\nCurrency\nUSD\nU.S. Dollar\n4,539.37\n","publishTime":"2026-05-17T12:10:00+08:00"},{"title":"Gold Price in U.S. Dollar Friday, 15 May 2026","