{"type":"message","id":"e6e99ee7","parentId":"695d355c","timestamp":"2026-05-17T19:07:17.958Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the network situation:\n- Binance: SSL error (connection reset) ❌\n- Yahoo Finance: HTTP 429 (rate limited, but connection works) ✅\n- Eastmoney: HTTP 404 (connection works, just 404 on root) ✅\n- Ainvest: HTTP 404 (connection works) ✅\n- Coze: timeout\n\nSo the VPS CAN connect to most services. The issue with yfinance was likely the curl_cffi TLS issue, not a network block. Let me try yfinance with standard requests instead of curl_cffi.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1872afe6ee4f4808bef3f042","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try yfinance with standard requests (not curl_cffi)\npython3 -c \"\nimport yfinance as yf\n# Force standard session\nyf.set_tz_cache_location(None)\nticker = yf.Ticker('AAPL', session=None)\nhist = ticker.history(period='5d')\nprint('AAPL via yfinance:')\nprint(hist[['Open','High','Low','Close']].to_string())\n\" 2>&1 | head -20","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":636,"output":382,"cacheRead":84736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":85754,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779044831694}}
